---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Report Abuse" description="How to report copyright, security, and other abuse concerns involving Portico.">
  <article class="legal-page section-light">
    <h1>Report abuse</h1>
    <p class="legal-lead">Portico respects privacy without ignoring credible harm. We review specific reports carefully and take action on the parts of the service we operate.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Send copyright, security, safety, and other abuse reports to <a href="mailto:abuse@getportico.tv">abuse@getportico.tv</a>. Please do not send passwords, access tokens, private keys, complete diagnostic archives, or unrelated personal information.</p>

    <h2>What to include</h2>
    <p>Help us understand the report by identifying the affected Portico account, invitation, hostname, URL, server, or other service element as precisely as you can. Describe the activity and why you believe it is unlawful, unsafe, or contrary to the Portico Terms. Include your name, a reliable way to contact you, and any supporting evidence that you are authorized to provide.</p>
    <p>For a copyright report, identify the protected work, the specific material or activity at issue, where it can be found, your relationship to the rightsholder, and a good-faith basis for the report. Include a statement that the information is accurate and your typed or electronic signature. We may ask for additional information required by applicable law before acting.</p>

    <h2>What happens next</h2>
    <p>We review sufficiently specific reports in good faith and consider the nature of the concern, the information available to Portico, the rights of affected people, and the role Portico actually plays. We may acknowledge the report, request clarification, notify the relevant account or server operator, preserve appropriate records, or refer the matter to a provider better positioned to address it.</p>
    <p>Where justified, Portico may limit or end hosted account, discovery, invitation, membership, device, or routing services connected to the reported activity. Repeated or egregious violations may result in loss of access to Portico-hosted services.</p>

    <h2>What Portico can and cannot access</h2>
    <p>Portico Cloud coordinates accounts and direct connections, but it does not host, relay, cache, inspect, or monitor media. Media, library information, and streaming activity remain on an independently operated Portico Server and travel directly between that server and its authorized clients. Portico therefore cannot search a private library, inspect a stream, or remove a file it does not possess.</p>
    <p>A report about media stored or transmitted by an independently operated server may need to be directed to that server's operator or network provider. Portico will still review whether its own hosted services are being misused.</p>

    <h2>Corrections and disputes</h2>
    <p>If you believe a report or action involving you was mistaken, reply to the notice or email <a href="mailto:abuse@getportico.tv">abuse@getportico.tv</a>. Identify the report or action, explain the correction, and include information supporting your position. We will review a good-faith response and restore or adjust hosted access when appropriate.</p>

    <h2>Urgent safety concerns</h2>
    <p>If someone is in immediate danger, contact local emergency services first. Law-enforcement and other lawful requests may also be sent to <a href="mailto:abuse@getportico.tv">abuse@getportico.tv</a> with official contact information and the applicable legal authority.</p>

    <h2>Privacy</h2>
    <p>We use report information to investigate, respond, maintain service security, and meet legal obligations. Information may be shared with the affected account or server operator, relevant providers, advisers, or authorities when reasonably necessary, subject to law and safety considerations. See our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> for more information.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
